# Copy to .env.local. Both settings are optional, the defaults are what you
# want for local development AND for exposing the app through ngrok.
#
# By default the browser calls /backend/* on this same origin, and the Next.js
# server proxies that to the FastAPI backend. That is what lets a phone use the
# app: the phone only ever talks to the address it loaded the page from.

# Where the *Next.js server* forwards /backend/* to. Resolved on the machine
# running `next dev` / `next start`, so localhost is correct here.
# Change it only if the backend is not on this machine or not on port 8000.
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# Set this ONLY to bypass the proxy and have the *browser* call a backend
# directly: the split-deployment case (frontend on Vercel, backend elsewhere).
# It must be reachable from the phone, and https if the page is https.
#
# Do NOT set it to http://localhost:8000. That works on your own machine and
# fails on every phone, because "localhost" there means the phone itself.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.com
